# Accepted / acknowledged container-image CVEs (trivy --ignorefile).
#
# Referenced by modules/monitoring/services/container-cve-exporter.nix via
# TRIVY_IGNOREFILE. Any CVE ID listed here is dropped from the per-image counts
# emitted to Prometheus, so it neither pages (ExposedImageFixableCriticalCVE /
# …HighCVE on shlink) nor shows in the Grafana digest gauges.
#
# Format: one public CVE identifier per line (e.g. CVE-2024-12345). Comments
# (# …) and blank lines are ignored. NO secrets ever belong in this file — CVE
# IDs are public references only.
#
# Workflow: after the first weekly scan, inspect the per-image JSON under
#   /var/lib/container-cve/reports/<name>.json   (0640 root:root)
# and add IDs here for CVEs you have evaluated and accepted (unfixable noise,
# not-applicable to our usage, or risk-accepted). Re-run:
#   sudo systemctl start container-cve-exporter.service
#
# Empty initially — populate after the baseline scan establishes which findings
# are real signal vs accepted noise.
